I set you down in the domain of the waters.
I set you down with the gāyatrī meter.
I set you down with the traiṣṭubha, with the jāgata, with the ānuṣṭubha, with the pāṅkta meter.
This one in the east is Bhūḥ;
his exhalation is Bhauvāyana;
spring is related to exhalation; the gāyatrī belongs to spring;
from the gāyatrī, the gāyatra [sāman];
from the gāyatra, the upāṃśu [cup];
from the upāṃśu, the trivṛt [stoma];
from the trivṛt, the rathantara [sāman];
Vasiṣṭha is the seer;
with you, held by Prajāpati, I take exhalation for the creatures.
This one in the south is Viśvakarman;
his mind is Vaiśvakarmaṇa;
summer is related to mind;
the triṣṭubh belongs to summer;
from the triṣṭubh, the svāra [sāman];
from the svāra, the antaryāma [cup];
from the antaryāma, the pañcadaśa [stoma];
from the pañcadaśa, the bṛhat [sāman];
Bharadvāja is the seer;
with you, held by Prajāpati, I take mind for the creatures.
This one in the west is Viśvavyacas;
his sight is Vaiśvavyacasa;
the rainy season is related to sight;
the jagatī belongs to the rainy season;
from the jagatī, the ṛksama [sāman];
from the ṛksama, the śukra [cup];
from the śukra, the saptadaśa [stoma];
from the saptadaśa, the vairūpa [sāman];
Jamadagni is the seer;
with you, held by Prajāpati, I take sight for the creatures.
This one in the north is Svar;
his hearing is Sauva;
autumn is related to hearing;
the anuṣṭubh belongs to autumn;
from the anuṣṭubh, the aiḍa [sāman];
from the aiḍa, the manthin [cup];
from the manthin, the ekaviṃśa [stoma];
from the ekaviṃśa, the vairāja [sāman];
Viśvāmitra is the seer;
with you, held by Prajāpati, I take hearing for the creatures.
This one above is Mati;
her speech is Mātyā;
winter is related to speech;
the paṅkti belongs to winter;
from the paṅkti, the nidhanavat [sāman];
from the nidhanavat, the āgrāyaṇa [cup];
from the āgrāyaṇa, the triṇava and trayastriṃśa [stomas];
from the triṇava and trayastriṃśa, the śākvara and raivata [sāmans];
Viśvakarman is the seer;
with you, held by Prajāpati, I take speech for the creatures.
Fill the space, fill the cleft; then sit firm;
Indra and Agni and Bṛhaspati have seated you in this womb.
These dappled cows, yielding milk for him, mix the Soma,
in the birth of the gods, the clans, in the three luminous spheres of heaven.

25.10.m:
Having a firm resting-place, having a firm womb, firm are you; sit upon the firm womb, O Sādhyā;
enjoying the first banner of the one in the pot, let the two Aśvins as Adhvaryus seat you here!
Nest-possessing, rich in ghee, bountiful, sit in the soft seat of the earth;
let the Rudras and Vasus praise you; swell these sacred formulations for good fortune;
let the two Aśvins as Adhvaryus seat you here!
With your own capacities, O father of capacity, sit here for the favor of the gods, for great delight;
be gracious as a father to a son; enter together with a body of good entry;
let the two Aśvins as Adhvaryus seat you here!
You are the loose earth of Agni, apsas by name; let all the gods praise you;
having the stoma as your back, rich in ghee, sit here; sacrifice for us possessions accompanied by offspring;
let the two Aśvins as Adhvaryus seat you here!
I set you down upon the back of Aditi, the supporter of the intermediate space, the prop of the quarters;
sovereign mistress of the worlds, wave, drop of the waters are you;
Viśvakarman is your seer; let the two Aśvins as Adhvaryus seat you here!
In union with the seasons, in union with the allocations, in union with the gods, in union with the gods that weave vitality,
for Agni Vaiśvānara;
let the two Aśvins as Adhvaryus seat you here!
In union with the seasons, in union with the allocations, in union with the Vasus, in union with the Rudras, in union with the Ādityas, in union with the All-Gods, in union with the gods that weave vitality,
for Agni Vaiśvānara;
let the two Aśvins as Adhvaryus seat you here!
Protect my exhalation, protect my diffused breath, protect my downward breath; make my sight shine far and wide; bring fame to my hearing;
swell the waters, invigorate the plants;
protect the two-footed, guard the four-footed; send down rain from heaven!

28.6.m:
Bright-light and Variegated-light;
True-light and Full-of-light;
True, and Order-guarding, and Transcending-distress;
Such-like and Otherwise-like;
Alike and Counter-alike;
Measured and Commensurate, and Bearing-together;
Cosmic Order and Truth;
Firm and Supporter;
Holder and Distributor, O Upholder;
Winning by Cosmic Order and Winning by Truth;
Conquering armies and Having good armies;
Near-enemy and Far-enemy troop.
Such ones, resembling these, come near to us;
alike ones, counter-alike ones, come!
Measured and commensurate ones, bearing together with us today, O Maruts, at this sacrifice!
The Maruts, the divine clans, became followers of Indra;
just as the Maruts, the divine clans, became followers of Indra, so may the divine clans and the human clans become followers of this sacrificer.

